# Pin what gets STORED in the repository to LF, regardless of each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting. Checkout is unaffected — a Windows working copy still
# gets CRLF — so this changes nothing day to day. What it prevents is a
# contributor with autocrlf=false committing CRLF and turning the next diff
# into a whole-file rewrite that buries the real change.
* text=auto

# Must be LF wherever they are checked out: CRLF breaks a shebang, and an
# Apple .p8 signing key with CRLF fails PEM parsing outright.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.p8   text eol=lf

# Apple root CA certificates are DER — treating them as text corrupts them and
# every signature check then fails for a reason nothing explains.
*.cer  binary
*.der  binary

# Never normalise.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary

# Generated — keep them out of diffs and out of language statistics.
package-lock.json  linguist-generated=true -diff
dist/**            linguist-generated=true
